course: dictionary
lesson: 10473
title: What is a tumour?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tumour is a lump in the body made of cells that grow when they should not. Cells usually grow and divide in an orderly way, but in a tumour they keep dividing out of control.
explain: Some tumours are harmless. Doctors call these benign. Others are cancer, and doctors call these malignant. Both kinds are lumps, so a doctor has to check which kind it is.
explain: Context helps you here. «Scientists have found tumours in sharks» tells you tumours can grow in animals too, not just in people. «A growth means a tumour, a lump that may or may not be cancer» tells you a growth is another word for a tumour.
fact: A tumour is a lump in the body made of cells that grow when they should not.
fact: A benign tumour is harmless. A malignant tumour is cancer.
fact: «Sharks can get cancer: scientists have found tumours (lumps of cancer) in sharks.»
fact: «A growth» is another word for a tumour, and it may or may not be cancer.
fact: «A shadow on the lung» means a mark on an X-ray that may be a tumour in the lung.
fact: In the Tasmanian devil, a face tumour disease has killed many, so disease-free groups are kept as insurance.
exercise: «Scientists have found tumours (lumps of cancer) in sharks.» What is a tumour? | A type of shark | *A lump in the body made of cells that grow when they should not | A bone in the jaw | A fish's fin
exercise: «"A growth" means a tumour, a lump that may or may not be cancer.» Which word means the same as tumour here? | marsupial | *growth | sharks | shadow
exercise: Some tumours are harmless. What is a harmless tumour called? | Malignant | Shadow | Brain | *Benign
test: «The Tasmanian devil has a face tumour disease that has killed many, so disease-free groups are kept as insurance.» Why are disease-free groups kept? | To make them bigger | *As insurance in case the disease kills the rest | To send them to the sea | To stop them being eaten
test: What is a malignant tumour? | *A lump of cancer | A type of shark | A kind of X-ray | A harmless lump
exam: «A shadow on the lung» means a mark on an X-ray that may be a tumour in the lung. What does this phrase suggest? | A bruise on the chest | A cough medicine | A shadow cast by the lungs | *A mark on an X-ray that may be a tumour
